{
  peppy_schema: "contract/v1",
  manifest: {
    name: "postures",
    tag: "v1",
    description: [
      "The whole-robot posture moves: a robot that can plan and execute a motion bringing every limb to a named posture.",
      "Two postures cover the operating loop:",
      "home: the rest posture with every gripper closed, the robot's natural pose to start from and power down at. For an arm, low and close to the robot's body.",
      "ready: the working posture, out in the robot's main workspace and poised to take commands. For an arm, raised out in front.",
      "The exact joint values behind each name are the implementer's business. Distinct from the streamed setpoints on the *_link pairings: these are discrete planned moves with a result.",
      "move_to_home first closes each gripper of the robot, then brings the arms to home. Where the arms can stop is a fact of the robot: on some robots, open jaws stop against the robot's body before the arms reach the rest posture. Thus no caller closes the grippers before it calls move_to_home. move_to_ready sends no command to the grippers.",
      "move_to_ready and move_to_home have the mark `moves_robot`: each MCP server, `peppy node call` and each lease holder asks the daemon (`robot_leases.check_move`) whether it may move the robot before it calls one of them.",
      "A posture goal is refused with `leader_streaming` while a leader streams a limb that the goal moves, and with `precondition_failed` while such a limb executes another move, and the message names the limb. move_to_ready moves the arms, and move_to_home moves the arms and the grippers. A leader is a robot commander, such as a leader arm or the browser panel, or the headset. A posture move completes once every arm stands at the posture, within the tolerance of the implementer. It fails with `timeout` when an arm does not stand there by the settle timeout of the implementer past the planned end, as when an object that the implementer does not see holds the arm short, and the message names the arm and how far it stands; with `rejected` when the joint limits cannot run it within 60 s, with `unreachable` when no plan brings an arm to the posture, with `resource_unavailable` when a limb stops answering, and with `attempt_failed` when it cannot go on for another reason. A failed goal gives no result. A cancelled goal, whether its caller or the stop of limb_motion cancelled it, gives the reason of the cancel and its result.",
      "Close rule of move_to_home: the close of a gripper ends as a gripper move of limb_motion ends: as soon as its jaws stand still, and at the latest at the settle timeout of the implementer, where they stand. A gripper that holds an item closes on it: its jaws stop on the item, and the arms go home with it. The close keeps the effort limit of the last command of the gripper, where the implementer limits the effort of a gripper, so a grasp keeps the effort that its caller gave it. A gripper that reports no state when its close starts gets no command: the goal leaves it as it stands and brings the arms home. The close takes at most 10 s: a goal whose close cannot end its travel in that time is refused with `rejected`, or fails with `timeout`. A cancel of the goal or a stop of limb_motion during the close, or between the close and the move of the arms, ends the goal cancelled before the arms move. A close that fails ends the goal with its failure, and the arms do not move. duration_s is the time of the arm move alone: the close adds its own time.",
      "Pose rule for the results: a result reports where each arm ended, as limb_state reports it, or no pose:",
      "Each pose is the grasp-point pose of an arm in the robot frame, which the result names in frame, at the result's timestamp, the time the implementer measured it. The description of limb_state defines the grasp point, and transforms defines the robot frame.",
      "The implementer measures the pose of every arm when the goal completes or ends cancelled, after the moves of all its arms ended.",
      "When an arm has no fresh measured pose then, arm_names and grasp_points are empty, frame is the robot frame, and timestamp is 0, since the result holds no measured value: the implementer never measured the joints of that arm, or their last measurement is stale.",
      "After a cancel or a stop, an arm that was still moving can come to rest away from the reported pose.",
    ],
  },
  failure_kinds: {
    unreachable: "No plan to the target",
    leader_streaming: "A leader streams a limb of the goal",
  },
  interfaces: {
    actions: [
      {
        name: "move_to_ready",
        description: "Bring the arms of the robot to ready, the working posture, on a motion that the implementer plans. The grippers get no command. The action gives no feedback. The result gives where each arm ended, per the pose rule of this contract.",
        goal_service: {
          request_message_format: {
            duration_s: { $type: "f64", $description: "Requested move duration (s), up to 60; floored at the duration the implementer's joint limits allow. 0 = fastest." },
          },
        },
        result_service: {
          response_message_format: {
            frame: { $type: "string", $description: "The frame of the record's values, as transforms names frames; a twist beside a child_frame is in child_frame, and a sensor's values are in frame through the sensor's own geometry." },
            timestamp: { $type: "time", $description: "The time of the record on the clock of transforms; 0 names the latest time in a command and every time in a report." },
            arm_names: { $type: "array", $items: "string", $description: "The implementer's arm names (e.g. \"left_arm\") in its fixed order, or none, per the pose rule of this contract." },
            grasp_points: {
              $type: "array",
              $description: "The measured grasp-point pose of each arm, in arm_names order, per the pose rule of this contract.",
              $items: {
                $type: "object",
                position: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $length: 3, $description: "x, y, z (m)." },
                orientation: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $length: 4, $description: "A unit quaternion [x, y, z, w]." },
              },
            },
          },
        },
        failure_kinds: ["unreachable", "leader_streaming"],
        marks: ["moves_robot"],
      },
      {
        name: "move_to_home",
        description: "Close each gripper of the robot, per the close rule of this contract, then bring the arms of the robot to home, the rest posture, on a motion that the implementer plans. The action gives no feedback. The result gives where each arm ended, per the pose rule of this contract.",
        goal_service: {
          request_message_format: {
            duration_s: { $type: "f64", $description: "Requested duration of the arm move (s), up to 60; floored at the duration the implementer's joint limits allow. 0 = fastest. The close of the grippers adds its own time, at most 10 s." },
          },
        },
        result_service: {
          response_message_format: {
            frame: { $type: "string", $description: "The frame of the record's values, as transforms names frames; a twist beside a child_frame is in child_frame, and a sensor's values are in frame through the sensor's own geometry." },
            timestamp: { $type: "time", $description: "The time of the record on the clock of transforms; 0 names the latest time in a command and every time in a report." },
            arm_names: { $type: "array", $items: "string", $description: "The implementer's arm names (e.g. \"left_arm\") in its fixed order, or none, per the pose rule of this contract." },
            grasp_points: {
              $type: "array",
              $description: "The measured grasp-point pose of each arm, in arm_names order, per the pose rule of this contract.",
              $items: {
                $type: "object",
                position: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $length: 3, $description: "x, y, z (m)." },
                orientation: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $length: 4, $description: "A unit quaternion [x, y, z, w]." },
              },
            },
          },
        },
        failure_kinds: ["unreachable", "leader_streaming"],
        marks: ["moves_robot"],
      },
    ],
  },
}
